     "body": "<p>When I create and ACL and navigate to it in the HTML UI, I am seeing the ACL content and properties. This appears to no longer be an issue.</p>\n\n<p>Steps:</p>\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>mvn jetty:run -pl fcrepo-webapp/</li>\n\t<li>curl -XPUT -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin  localhost:8080/rest/box  -i</li>\n\t<li>curl -XPUT -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -H\"Content-Type: text/turtle\" --data-binary @acl.ttl localhost:8080/rest/box/fcr:acl  -i</li>\n\t<li>Where acl.ttl is:<br/>\n   ```<br/>\n   @prefix acl: &lt;<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#</a>&gt;.<br/>\n   &lt;#authz&gt; a acl:Authorization;<br/>\n      acl:accessTo &lt;/rest/box&gt;;<br/>\n      acl:agent \"user1\";<br/>\n      acl:mode acl:Read.<br/>\n   ```</li>\n\t<li>Open browser to: <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/box/fcr:acl\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/box/fcr:acl</a> &#8211; all good</li>\n</ul>\n",
     "created": "18/Nov/20 8:16 PM",
